<title>SPAIN: Spain's SEPI names two new heads at Fecsa.</title>
<headline>Spain's SEPI names two new heads at Fecsa.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish state holding company SEPI on Friday appointed two new members to the board of directors of electricity firm Fuerzas Electricas de Cataluna (Fecsa).</p>
<p>A statement said these were Albert Mitja and Josep Lluis Vilaseca. No further details were given.</p>
<p>At the end of May 1996 the company appointed Juan Echevarria Puig as chairman.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
